%I A037292 #13 Oct 19 2026 10:48:08
%S A037292 1,2,2,55,2,4,2,801288,165,4,2,110,2,4,4
%N A037292 Number of nonassociative rings with n elements.
%C A037292 The standard definition of a ring requires that multiplication be associative, so these are very nonstandard rings.
%C A037292 The rings need not contain a multiplicative unit.
%C A037292 In fact more is known: 1,2,2,55,2,4,2,801288,165,4,2,110,2,4,4,?,2,330,2,110,4,4,2,1602576.
%C A037292 This sequence may be multiplicative. - _Mitch Harris_, Apr 19 2005
%H A037292 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Ring.html">Ring</a>.
%Y A037292 Cf. A027623.
%K A037292 nonn,more,changed
%O A037292 1,2
%A A037292 _Christian G. Bower_, Jun 15 1998
